EXT. SKY-WHALE MARKET - FLOATING DECK - DAWN

A vast whale drifts through pink clouds, its back lashed with rope bridges and canvas stalls. Lanterns burn in the morning. Merchants shout in the distance.

MIRABEL "MIMSY" ASHGROVE, 20s, a thief in a patchwork cloak, crouches on a spice barrel. A copper compass spins in her fist.

GIDEON "GID" THORNE, 30s, in the livery of the Harbor Guard, climbs the barrel stack behind her. His boots slap the planks.

GID
Mimsy. Don't.

MIMSY
Gid.

GID
Put it down.

MIMSY
It was mine first.

GID
It belonged to the Admiral.

MIMSY
The Admiral is dead.

GID
That doesn't make it yours.

Mimsy tosses the compass from hand to hand. He winces at each toss.

MIMSY
(to herself)
Steady, girl. Steady.

GID
Who are you talking to?

MIMSY
Nobody.

She stands on the barrel. Spreads her arms to the whole market below. The merchants glance up.

MIMSY (CONT'D)
(loudly, to the crowd)
Good people of the Whale! This man would take my inheritance!

A murmur. A woman drops a basket of figs. A boy points.

GID
(to the crowd)
Nothing of the sort! Return to your stalls!

MIMSY
He's a liar!

GID
She's a thief!

MIMSY
Both can be true.

Gid lunges. Mimsy leaps. They collide midair and crash through the canvas roof of the fruit stall, tumbling in a heap of melons and rope.

Both lie flat for a second. Then both scramble upright, glaring, each with one hand on the compass.

GID (CONT'D)
Let go, Mimsy.

MIMSY
You first, Gid.

They pull. The compass spins. The needle jerks west, then stops, pointing straight down at the clouds beneath the whale.

Both freeze. They look at the needle. Then at each other.

MIMSY (CONT'D)
(quietly)
Oh.

GID
It's pointing at the sea.

MIMSY
It's pointing at something under the sea.

The whale rumbles, a long, deep note that shakes the stalls. The lanterns sway. The merchants scatter, tipping carts.

GID
Run?

MIMSY
Run.

They pull the compass between them like a rope and sprint for the bow.
